msgid "Full mode (`-G`) supports inspecting:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/error-handling-and-debugging.md:340
msgid "local variables and arguments rustc exposes through `var_debug_info`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/error-handling-and-debugging.md:341
msgid "scalar types (`bool`, integers, floats), raw pointers, and references"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/error-handling-and-debugging.md:342
msgid ""
"structs, tuples, and fixed-size arrays, with their fields shown at the "
"correct (real-layout) offsets, e.g. `out = DisjointSlice {ptr: 0x..., len: 1}"
"` and `idx = ThreadIndex {raw: 0}`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/error-handling-and-debugging.md:346
msgid ""
"End-to-end behavior (breakpoint binds, backtrace, `info args`/`info locals`) "
"is checked on real hardware by `scripts/debug-smoketest.sh`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/error-handling-and-debugging.md:349
msgid ""
"Full mode does **not** yet describe: enums (`Option`, `Result`, and other "
"multi-variant types), bare slice arguments split into a `(ptr, len)` pair at "
"the ABI boundary, closures, projections like `x.0`, or destructured "
"variables. Locals of an inlined helper frame may also show fewer entries "
"than the kernel frame; select the kernel frame (`frame 1`) to inspect kernel "
"locals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/error-handling-and-debugging.md:355
msgid "Breakpoint workflow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/error-handling-and-debugging.md:357
msgid "Build with debug: `cargo oxide debug <example>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/error-handling-and-debugging.md:358
msgid "Set a breakpoint on your kernel: `break vecadd`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/error-handling-and-debugging.md:359
msgid "Run: `run`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/error-handling-and-debugging.md:360
msgid "Inspect threads: `cuda thread`, `cuda block`, `cuda warp`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/error-handling-and-debugging.md:361
msgid "Print variables: `print idx`, `print *c_elem`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/error-handling-and-debugging.md:363
msgid ""
"`cargo oxide debug` selects the executable from Cargo's build artifact "
"metadata instead of assuming `target/release/<example>`. That keeps "
"debugging working with custom binary names, `package.default-run`, "
"configured target directories, host target triples, and virtual workspaces. "
"Use `--bin <name>` when a package has multiple binaries and no unambiguous "
"default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/error-handling-and-debugging.md:369
msgid ""
"For programmatic breakpoints, use `debug::breakpoint()` in your kernel code. "
"When cuda-gdb hits the `brkpt` instruction, it pauses execution and lets you "
"inspect the GPU state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/error-handling-and-debugging.md:374
msgid ""
"`debug::breakpoint()` will **crash** the kernel if no debugger is attached. "
"Guard it with a compile-time flag or only use it during debugging sessions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/error-handling-and-debugging.md:378
msgid "`cargo oxide sanitize` -- Compute Sanitizer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/error-handling-and-debugging.md:380
msgid ""
"For memory and synchronization correctness checks, run the same build path "
"under NVIDIA Compute Sanitizer:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/error-handling-and-debugging.md:383
msgid ""
"cargo oxide sanitize vecadd\n"
"cargo oxide sanitize sharedmem --tool racecheck\n"
"cargo oxide sanitize debug --tool synccheck -- --kernel-name kns=clock\n"
"cargo oxide sanitize my_app -- --leak-check full -- --app-flag value\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/error-handling-and-debugging.md:390
msgid ""
"`memcheck` is the default tool. Use `racecheck` for shared-memory hazards, "
"`initcheck` for uninitialized global-memory reads, and `synccheck` for "
"invalid synchronization usage. Extra arguments after `--` are passed "
"directly to `compute-sanitizer` before the executable; use a second `--` to "
"pass arguments to the target program after the executable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/error-handling-and-debugging.md:396
msgid ""
"The command enables optimized device line tables by default so findings can "
"name Rust source files and lines. An explicit `CUDA_OXIDE_DEBUG` process or "
"project setting still wins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/error-handling-and-debugging.md:400
msgid ""
"Compute Sanitizer normally exits with status zero even when it reports a "
"tool finding. `cargo oxide sanitize` therefore supplies `--error-exitcode "
"86` by default, making findings fail scripts and CI. An explicit sanitizer "
"argument overrides that default:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/error-handling-and-debugging.md:405
msgid ""
"# Intentionally keep a zero exit status and inspect the printed report.\n"
"cargo oxide sanitize vecadd -- --error-exitcode 0\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/error-handling-and-debugging.md:410
msgid ""
"Options such as `--check-exit-code no` and `--require-cuda-init no` weaken "
"what a zero status proves. The wrapper therefore never declares the report "
"clean from process status alone; it reports completion and leaves the "
"sanitizer output visible for inspection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/error-handling-and-debugging.md:415
msgid ""
"The `--no-fmad` CLI flag is forwarded through both ordinary and interop "
"builds. It keeps ordinary multiply and add/subtract operations separate, "
"with one rounding per operation. Explicit fused operations such as `f32::"
"mul_add` remain fused."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/error-handling-and-debugging.md:420
msgid ""
"NVVM IR and LTOIR builds also produce `.options` and versioned `.target` "
"sidecars. Keep both files with the artifact so later libNVVM and nvJitLink "
"steps preserve the same FMA policy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/error-handling-and-debugging.md:424
msgid ""
"Run `memcheck` first when investigating memory safety. The other tools are "
"complementary and do not perform full memory-access checking."
msgstr ""

